Links 2.30 for PsiWeb (web/links). Applied by web/links/fetch.sh.
- drivers.c, links.h, main.c: the "psi" graphics driver (GRDRV_PSI), always graphics mode
- img.c (PSI_LAZY_IMAGES): no decoder or full-size buffer kept for pictures not yet drawn;
  during layout a JPEG is read only up to its size (phase 3)
- jpeg.c (PSI_JPEG_SCALE): libjpeg scales while decoding; buffered mode only for progressive;
  colour JPEGs decoded to grey (Y only), fast IDCT; a progressive JPEG takes in all the
  data there is before showing a scan (phase 3)
- html.c (PSIWEB): no <link rel=canonical/alternate/...> lines, no prefetch/preload
- html.c, html_r.c (PSIWEB): the form search for each control no longer starts at the top of
  the page when there is no <form> (quadratic: 200M ARM instructions on BBC)
- links.h, session.c, view.c, view_gr.c (PSI_NO_BARS, with GRDRV_PSI): no title or status
  bar, the page gets the whole screen; no welcome box; a tap at the top is on the page
- dip.c (PSIWEB): fixed-point glyph sharpening, a glyph lookup cache, remembered colours,
  the last picture gamma table kept (soft-float costs on the ARM710)
- connect.c, https.c, default.c (PSI_EPOC, the ARM build): connections through
  web/links/epoc/psi_os.c (pwn: psiglue + TLS 1.3), 16 KB reads, no config files
Phase 3 (speed; see PORTING.md, "Phase 3: performance"):
- html.c, html_tbl.c (PSIWEB): fast paths in the parser (script/style bodies and plain text
  skipped with memchr, element names' lengths kept, word-at-a-time attribute scanning), a
  memo of the current element's attributes for get_attr_val, values copied in one go
- dip.c (PSIWEB): run-length glyphs (web/links/mkfont.py --rle), widths kept per font size,
  scaler divisions by reciprocal, exact /255 without a divide; (PSI_EPOC) the sRGB picture
  gamma table made at build time (web/links/mkdither.py); the colour scaler divides by
  reciprocal (Granlund-Montgomery, exact)
- dither.c (PSI_EPOC): the screen's colour tables made at build time (mkdither.py)
- compress.c (PSIWEB): no CRC check of gzip bodies (TLS or TCP has checked them)
- sched.c (PSIWEB): each connection's host, port and keepalive key parsed once

